  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Bookshop Window",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Bookshop Window\"**\n\nMultimage shows real books at the size a shop window gives them. The cover is the colour source: each featured book sits on a full-width field tinted from its own cover, tilted a few degrees, throwing a shadow in a darker shade of the same hue. Everything around it stays quiet and institutional: a navy frame (header, footer, newsletter band), white reading surfaces, Playfair Display titles in navy, Inter for everything a reader acts on.\n\nThe system is flat and square. Every corner resolves to 0px at the token level, depth comes from tone (navy frame, white page, mist hover, cover-tinted fields) and from the one soft navy shadow, never from stacked cards. One action colour, a deep burnt orange, carries the primary step on any surface; links and secondary steps stay navy.\n\nThe voice is a volunteer publisher's, not a store's: proof is the book itself (cover, title, author, price, ways to get it), not badges or invented numbers.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cover-tinted fields derived from each image's own DatoCMS colours.",
      "Square corners everywhere (0px radius, enforced in the theme).",
      "Navy frame, white page, deep orange for the one primary action.",
      "Playfair Display headings in navy over Inter text in charcoal.",
      "44px minimum tap targets on every interactive element."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Cover Is the Colour Rule",
        "body": "A book's surface takes its colour from its own cover through `src/lib/colors.ts`; never pick a decorative hue for a book block by hand.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Orange Rule",
        "body": "Burnt Action Orange marks the single primary action of a block. Secondary actions are mist with navy text; further ways are navy underlined links.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The White-on-Orange-Deep Rule",
        "body": "White text sits on brand-orange-deep, never on brand-orange.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Title Is the Heading Rule",
        "body": "Nothing sits stacked above a heading: no kicker, eyebrow or tag line. Context goes below the title (subtitle, author) or into a caption (\"Il libro del momento\" is a figcaption under the cover).",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Serif Is for Published Things Rule",
        "body": "Playfair carries titles, prices and the size of the catalogue (the slate size line under the h1, the result count); actions, meta and navigation stay in Inter.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Only the Book Floats Rule",
        "body": "The cover is the one object allowed to cast a strong, coloured shadow and to tilt (4deg hero, 5deg featured block). Containers stay flat. On a book card only the cover moves on hover (rises 6px, 300ms ease-out, motion-safe); the card itself does not lift.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do derive a book block's colours from its cover through `pickBaseColor`, `lightenColor` and `darkenColor` in `src/lib/colors.ts`.",
      "Do keep corners square; rely on the theme's 0px radius rather than adding literal radii.",
      "Do use brand-orange-deep for the one primary action and navy underlined links for further ways.",
      "Do give every interactive element at least 44px of height on touch screens.",
      "Do set `[--focus-ring:var(--color-white)]` on dark surfaces and `hover:text-white focus:text-white` on links inside them.",
      "Do put context under a title (subtitle, author, caption), never above it.",
      "Do put a book's status (anno, Ebook, Fuori catalogo) in its slate meta line.",
      "Do keep a surface's orange-deep to its one primary action; utility toggles are navy, secondary steps white-outlined or mist."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't put white text on brand-orange (#fa7810); it is 2.7:1.",
      "Don't use brand-sky for text or behind white text; it is decorative only. Links are navy, underlined inside running text.",
      "Don't stack a kicker, eyebrow or tag label above a heading.",
      "Don't add literal border radii (`rounded-[2rem]`, `border-radius: 9999px`); they bypass the square theme.",
      "Don't add `focus:outline-hidden` with a private ring; the global `:focus-visible` outline is the one indicator.",
      "Don't tilt or shadow anything but a book cover.",
      "Don't lift or outline a book card on hover; only its cover rises.",
      "Don't set a ribbon, badge or price chip on a book card."
    ]
  }
